Package syscall on Radix (ADR 0350): every function is a C library call,
generated from //sys lines by mksyscall.pl -radix as on OpenBSD, with
mlibc's types and constants (Linux's) made by cgo -godefs and
mkerrors.sh, which reads the error and signal texts from mlibc's source,
as a program for Radix cannot run on the build machine. Syscall and
RawSyscall return ENOSYS: Radix has no system call numbers. Processes
start with the C library's fork and execve; there is no ptrace. Dukovo
only.

